# Force LF line endings for files that run inside the Linux container,
# regardless of the contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Without
# this, checking this repo out on Windows (core.autocrlf=true, the
# default) silently converts entrypoint.sh to CRLF, which breaks its
# shebang inside the container: "exec /app/entrypoint.sh: no such file or
# directory" — a very confusing error for something that looks fine in an
# editor.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
